        ["A patient with C5 tetraplegia becomes lightheaded and pale when the tilt table is raised to 45°. What is the BEST immediate response?",["Lower the table toward horizontal and monitor BP","Raise the table to 80° to build upright tolerance","Have the patient perform a Valsalva maneuver","Remove the abdominal binder and stockings"],"These are signs of orthostatic hypotension. Lowering the table restores cerebral perfusion; tilt is then progressed gradually with binder and compression in place."]
