        ["A patient with Bell's palsy cannot fully close the right eye. Which intervention is the PRIORITY?",["Protect the eye with lubrication and nighttime taping","Forceful mass facial movements against resistance","Vigorous ice massage over the facial nerve","Daily high-intensity e-stim to the forehead"],"Incomplete eye closure risks corneal injury, so eye protection comes first. Forceful mass movement may promote synkinesis."]
